• US-001 is now complete. Here's a summary of what was implemented:

  Summary

  Story Completed: US-001 - Create tx-recovery.ts module with types and storage

  Files Created/Modified:

  1. src/model/cashu/tx-recovery.ts - New transaction recovery module with:
    • TxType type: 'nutszap' | 'nutszap-melt' | 'zap'
    • TxState interface with all required fields (txId, type, timestamps, step,
      ms, proofs, quotes, nostr, errors)
    • Step constants for all three transaction flows (NUTSZAP_STEPS, NUTSZAP_MEL
      EPS, ZAP_STEPS)
    • IndexedDB storage functions: saveTxState, loadTxState, deleteTxState, list
      ingTransactions, listAllTransactions
    • activeTxIdStore using persistentWritable for localStorage tracking
    • Helper functions: generateTxId, createTxState, isTxFinalized, addTxError,
      teTxStep
  2. prd.json - Updated to mark US-001 as passing
  3. progress.txt - Added progress entry with learnings for future iterations

  Key Design Decisions:

  • Used IndexedDB for durable transaction state storage (larger capacity, bette
    for structured data)
  • Used localStorage (via persistentWritable) for simple active transaction ID
    acking
  • Comprehensive TxState interface captures everything needed for crash recover
  • Error tracking includes retryable flag for smart retry logic
  • Step constants use as const for proper TypeScript literal type inference

